\par\par \b \uc2  Nigeria frees  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  rates. \b0\par\par\uc2 496 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LAGOS (Reuter) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Nigeria (CBN) said on Thursday that commercial and merchant banks were free to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at market rates, effectively ending one year of fixed exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  The Inter-bank Market (IFEM) will operate at rates mutually agreed between buyers and sellers of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,'' the CBN said in its guideline for the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system announced by the government on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the CBN withdrew 10 billion naira from the banking system in what one dealer described as an attempt to weaken demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and ensure the naira started off with a good rate when autonomous market trading began. \par \par \uc2  The CBN said the official rate would remain at 22 naira to the dollar, a fraction of the parallel market rate. The official rate will only apply to certain government transactions. \par \par \uc2  The private sector and government parastatals run on a commercialised basis must now source their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the autonomous market. \par \par \uc2  Banks had not started trading pending release of the guidelines but bankers said the new policy amounted to a devaluation of the naira and the floating of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It is a float of the naira, but the government is just not prepared to say this,'' a senior Lagos-based banker said. \par \par \uc2  When asked by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the week what rate they were likely to fix for the dollar, banks quoted around 80 naira to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- close to the black market rate. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the autonomous market will be based on free market principles. From time to time the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Inter-Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market in order to achieve the desired policy objectives including exchange rate stability, through buying from and selling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to authorised dealers,'' the CBN guidelines said. \par \par \uc2  The CBN said only authorised dealers and bureaux de change could trade in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The black market remains illegal. \par \par \uc2  Banks reopen for business on Friday at 8 a.m. (0700 GMT). \par \par \uc2  Financial operators said the CBN on Wednesday issued commercial and merchant banks with compulsory stabilisation securities totalling 10 billion naira. \par \par \uc2  The CBN appears to be trying to make sure the naira starts off with a good rate when the autonomous market opens,'' said an official of one Lagos-based discount house. \par \par \uc2  The CBN stopped issuing compulsory stabilisation securities in 1993 when it began voluntary weekly sales of treasury bills. \par \par \uc2  Under the new system, the CBN will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  from time to time in the autonomous market by buying and selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at market rates. \par \par \uc2  Banks earlier this week sought to cash in their treasury bills in anticipation of CBN's first hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sale, financial operators said. \par \par \uc2  Financial analysts say the naira is likely to come under pressure in 1995 unless the CBN can either squeeze banks of excess cash or increase available \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr1k05od7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
