\par\par \b \uc2  Nigeria allows free  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LAGOS, Jan 14 (Reuter) - Nigeria said on Saturday it would permit an autonomous \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the country, a major relaxation of its tightly controlled economy. \par \par \uc2  Announcing this in his 1995 radio and television budget broadcast, military ruler General Sani Abacha said this was to allow a free flow of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the country. \par \par \uc2  He also repealed the 1962 Exchange Control Act and the 1989 Enterprises Promotion Decree which barred foreigners from holding majority stakes in many businesses. \par \par \uc2  The Exchange Control Act restricts the movement of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in and out of Nigeria and prohibits the transfer of securities outside the country. \par \par \uc2  The Enterprises Promotion Decree prevents foreigners from taking majority stake in some categories of companies in Nigeria. \par \par \uc2  The removal of the two laws should significantly open up Nigeria's equity market to foreign participation. \par \par \uc2  "Government shall examine all laws, regulations, rules, etc that hinder the free flow of investments and funds into Nigeria," Abacha said. \par \par \uc2  He added: "Such rules will be repealed and the regulations relaxed." \par \par \uc2  The measures mark a return to free market reforms which Nigeria abandoned in Abacha's first budget in January 1994 after he seized power in November, 1993. \par \par \uc2  In that budget, he fixed the naira exchange rate at 22 to the dollar, a fraction of its illegal but thriving black-market level, and capped interest rates at 21 percent. \par \par \uc2  The policy led to a big reduction in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflow to Nigeria. \par \par \uc2  In the new budget he said "the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will henceforth be subject to guided delegulation, as shall interest rate regime." \par \par \uc2  "The exchange rate policy in 1995 is designed to maintain the current official rate and at the same time permit the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the autonomous market," Abacha said. \par \par \uc2  "To this end, the autonomous market will now be permitted in Nigeria and the inter-bank autonomous market shall be allowed to operate freely," he added. \par \par \uc2  Abacha said the government had retained the 22 naira to the dollar official exchange rate but suspended hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at the official market. \par \par \uc2  It was not immediately clear what the relationship between the official and the autonomous markets would be. \par \par \uc2  The finance minister is due to explain how the the new \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will operate when he gives the budget breakdown on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On interest rates, Abacha said there would be modifications to allow flexibility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  of last year's policy. \par \par \uc2  "Under the new arrangements, banks and other financial institutions are required to maintain a maximum spread of 7.5 percent between their deposit and lending rates subject to a maximum lending rate of 21 percent," Abacha said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr1e089k5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
